{% import "macros.njk" as m %}

<div class="calc">
  <div class="inputs">
    {{ m.field('cost', 'What it costs today', '₹', 10000, 100000000, 10000, 1500000, '₹10k', '₹10 Cr') }}
    {{ m.field('n', 'Years until you need it', 'years', 1, 40, 1, 10, '1 yr', '40 yrs') }}
    {{ m.field('inf', 'Inflation on this goal', '%', 0, 15, 0.5, 6, '0%', '15%') }}
    {{ m.field('r', 'Expected return (p.a.)', '%', 4, 20, 0.5, 12, '4%', '20%') }}
    {{ m.field('have', 'Already saved', '₹', 0, 100000000, 10000, 0, '₹0', '₹10 Cr') }}
    <div class="result-actions"><button class="btn-ghost" data-copylink>Copy link to this calculation</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="results">
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat hero"><div class="k">Monthly investment needed</div><div class="v" id="out-sip">—</div><div class="sub" id="out-sip-sub"></div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="k">Goal will cost</div><div class="v" id="out-fc">—</div><div class="sub">inflated to your date</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="k">You invest in total</div><div class="v" id="out-inv">—</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="k">Growth contributes</div><div class="v pos" id="out-gain">—</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat" id="mix-box" style="border-left:4px solid var(--accent);">
      <div class="k" id="mix-label">Suggested mix</div>
      <div class="v" id="mix-title" style="font-size:1.05rem;">—</div>
      <div class="sub" id="mix-text"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-goal"></canvas></div>
    <p class="chart-note">Your fund building towards the inflated cost of the goal.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<article class="article">
  <h2>Short term, medium term, long term</h2>
  <p>The single most useful question in goal planning is not which fund to buy — it is how long you have. The horizon decides how much risk the money can carry, because risk is only survivable if there is time to recover from it. Equity markets fall sharply every few years; whether that is an inconvenience or a disaster depends entirely on whether your deadline arrives before the recovery does.</p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Horizon</th><th>Typical mix</th><th>Where it usually sits</th><th>Planning return</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Under 3 years</th><td>100% debt</td><td>RD, FD, liquid or short-duration debt funds</td><td>6–7%</td></tr>
        <tr><th>3–5 years</th><td>~30% equity</td><td>Conservative hybrid or balanced-advantage funds</td><td>8–9%</td></tr>
        <tr><th>5–7 years</th><td>~50–60% equity</td><td>Balanced or aggressive hybrid funds</td><td>9–11%</td></tr>
        <tr><th>7–10 years</th><td>~70% equity</td><td>Index and flexi-cap funds, with a debt component</td><td>11%</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Over 10 years</th><td>80–100% equity</td><td>Diversified equity: index, flexi-cap, mid-cap</td><td>11–12%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="chart-note">Indicative allocations for a typical investor. Your own risk tolerance and other assets should adjust these — they are a starting point, not advice.</p>

  <h2>How this is calculated</h2>
  <p>Two steps. First the goal is inflated to the year you need it, because today's price is not what you will pay:</p>
  <div class="formula">Future cost = today's cost × (1 + inflation)<sup>years</sup></div>
  <p>Then anything already saved is grown at your expected return, subtracted, and the shortfall is converted into a monthly instalment:</p>
  <div class="formula">Monthly investment = shortfall ÷ [ ((1 + i)<sup>n</sup> − 1) ÷ i × (1 + i) ]</div>

  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>A wedding you would budget ₹15 lakh for today, ten years away, with 6% inflation. The real target is about <strong>₹26.86 lakh</strong>, not ₹15 lakh. At a 12% expected return that needs roughly <strong>₹11,560 a month</strong> — of which about ₹13.9 lakh is your own contribution and the rest is growth.</p>
  <p>Plan against the uninflated ₹15 lakh instead and you would invest about ₹6,460 a month, arriving with ₹15 lakh against a ₹26.86 lakh bill — short by more than ₹11 lakh. That gap is precisely what inflation compounds to over ten years, and it is the most common failure in goal planning.</p>

  <h2>Making the plan hold</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Keep goals separate.</strong> One SIP per goal makes it obvious whether each is on track, and stops a near-term need quietly consuming a long-term fund.</li>
    <li><strong>Fund the emergency buffer first.</strong> Six months of expenses in a liquid account is what prevents every surprise from derailing a goal.</li>
    <li><strong>Raise the amount as income grows.</strong> A plan set once and never revisited falls behind. Stepping contributions up annually is the easiest correction available — see the <a href="/step-up-sip-calculator/">step-up SIP calculator</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>De-risk as the date nears.</strong> Shift gradually from equity to debt over the final three years rather than hoping the market cooperates on the week you need the money.</li>
    <li><strong>Review once a year.</strong> Compare the fund value against the plan and correct early, while corrections are still small.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Specific goals</h2>
  <p>Some goals have their own dynamics and their own calculators here: <a href="/child-education-calculator/">children's education</a> uses a higher inflation rate than ordinary spending, <a href="/retirement-calculator/">retirement</a> has to fund decades of withdrawals rather than a single purchase, and <a href="/emi-calculator/">a home</a> usually involves a loan alongside the deposit you save.</p>
</article>

<script>
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
  var MIXES = [
    { max: 3,   title: 'Short term — stay in debt',        text: 'Under 3 years: RDs, FDs, liquid or short-duration debt funds. Equity can fall sharply and may not recover before your deadline. Expect roughly 6–7%.' },
    { max: 5,   title: 'Short-to-medium — mostly debt',    text: '3–5 years: around 30% equity via a conservative hybrid or balanced-advantage fund, the rest in debt. Expect roughly 8–9%.' },
    { max: 7,   title: 'Medium term — balanced',           text: '5–7 years: roughly half equity, half debt, typically through a balanced or aggressive hybrid fund. Expect roughly 9–11%.' },
    { max: 10,  title: 'Long term — equity-led',           text: '7–10 years: about 70% equity in index and flexi-cap funds, with a debt component for stability. Expect roughly 11%.' },
    { max: 999, title: 'Very long term — equity',          text: 'Over 10 years: 80–100% diversified equity. There is time to absorb several market cycles, and inflation is the bigger risk than volatility. Expect roughly 11–12%.' }
  ];

  function recalc() {
    var cost = CM.val('cost'), n = Math.round(CM.val('n'));
    var inf = CM.val('inf') / 100, r = CM.val('r') / 100, have = CM.val('have');
    if (cost <= 0 || n <= 0) return;

    var fc = cost * Math.pow(1 + inf, n);
    var haveFv = have * Math.pow(1 + r, n);
    var gap = Math.max(0, fc - haveFv);
    var i = r / 12, months = n * 12;
    var sip = i === 0 ? gap / months : gap / (((Math.pow(1 + i, months) - 1) / i) * (1 + i));
    var invested = sip * months + have;

    CM.set('out-sip', gap <= 0 ? 'Already funded ✓' : CM.inr(sip));
    CM.set('out-sip-sub', gap <= 0 ? 'existing savings cover it' : 'for ' + n + ' years at ' + CM.num(CM.val('r'), 1) + '%');
    CM.set('out-fc', CM.inr(fc));
    CM.set('out-inv', CM.inr(invested));
    CM.set('out-gain', CM.inr(Math.max(0, fc - invested)));

    var mix = MIXES.find(function (x) { return n <= x.max; });
    CM.set('mix-label', 'Suggested mix for ' + n + ' ' + (n === 1 ? 'year' : 'years'));
    CM.set('mix-title', mix.title);
    CM.set('mix-text', mix.text);

    var labels = [], fund = [], target = [], bal = have;
    for (var y = 0; y <= n; y++) {
      labels.push('Y' + y);
      fund.push(bal);
      target.push(cost * Math.pow(1 + inf, y));
      if (y < n) bal = bal * (1 + r) + sip * 12 * (1 + r);
    }
    CM.lineChart('chart-goal', labels, [
      { label: 'Your fund', data: fund, role: '--s1', fill: true },
      { label: 'Goal cost', data: target, role: '--s3' }
    ]);
  }
  CM.bind(['cost', 'n', 'inf', 'r', 'have'], recalc);
});
</script>
